WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.590
Course completion is not capability. A record saying someone watched a module answers a question nobody outside the classroom is asking.

2
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:20.460
What is needed is evidence a sceptical reader can inspect: which competency, backed by which piece of work, recorded when, and still standing now.

3
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:28.260
The learner command centre. Solid on the skill wheel is what has been verified, not what has been attempted.

4
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:36.350
Six steps from a lesson to a portfolio, and it matters which of them are automatic and which are deliberately not.

5
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:45.420
A self-claim and a piece of applied work are not weighted the same, because a claim is not proof.

6
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:54.480
Every write is idempotency-keyed, and a record that can be revised after the fact is a claim rather than evidence.

7
00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:04.950
That makes the operation idempotent by construction: running it twice produces the same state, rather than counting the same work twice.

8
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:13.960
Two independent gates. Collapsing them into one would let approval imply consent, or consent imply approval.

9
00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:24.760
Updating a competency the instant a submission lands was considered and not pursued. The record says so rather than implying the loop is closed.

10
00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:30.040
Every claim on the page is pinned to a commit you can open.
